# Line endings.
#
# The repository stores LF and checks out LF, on every platform. This matches
# `"endOfLine": "lf"` in .prettierrc — without it, a `core.autocrlf=true` clone
# checks files out as CRLF, Prettier rewrites them to LF, and every touched file
# shows a whole-file diff that is pure line endings and no content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are read by cmd.exe, which wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# UTF-16LE, so it contains NUL bytes. Marked non-text because line-ending
# normalisation would corrupt the encoding.
.env.example -text

# Binary assets — never normalised, never shown as text diffs.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Generated: keep out of diffs and language stats.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
